    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Primary Ability:</strong> Dexterity</p><p><em>“If reality needs a signature to let hope through the checkpoint, you’re the one who forges it.”</em></p><p>Phantom Couriers are quantum-phase messengers who slip between the edges of timelines to deliver what must arrive. They aren’t just fast—they are <em>misaligned</em> with cause-and-effect in ways that make interception a suggestion instead of a rule.</p><p>On the tactical map, a Phantom Courier is a hyper-mobile skirmisher and route-runner: stitching the battlefield together, baiting attacks into empty air, and getting critical things out of danger. On the strategic layer, they’re the reason Intrigue operations finish with everybody saying, “Wait, <em>how</em> did that get here?”</p><hr /><h3>Class Features by Tier (BBTTCC Overlay)</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Tier 1 — Phase-Slip Initiate.</strong><br />You gain proficiency in <em>Stealth</em> and <em>Acrobatics</em>. When you travel with a party, the <strong>first terrain hazard each segment is ignored</strong> as long as you are conscious and actively running the route.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 2 — Operation Ghost Dividend.</strong><br />When you successfully complete an <em>Infiltration</em> scenario where you personally participated, your faction <strong>refunds 1 Intrigue OP</strong> that was spent on that operation (minimum 0).</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 3 — Evasive Echo.</strong><br />You gain an <em>Evasion</em>-style benefit: succeeding on a Dexterity save vs half damage means <strong>no damage</strong>, and a failed save means <strong>half damage</strong>. You exist at several slightly different coordinates when danger hits.</p></li><li><p><strong>Tier 4 — Dimensional Flicker.</strong><br />Once you’re fully online, you can use a <strong>bonus action each turn</strong> to <strong>teleport up to 30 feet</strong> to a space you can see, without provoking opportunity attacks. You don’t run through battlefields—you redraw your outline.</p></li></ul><hr /><h3>Phantom Courier Progression (Highlights)</h3><ul><li><strong>1st Level:</strong> Phase-Slip Initiate, Ghoststep Reflexes.</li><li><strong>2nd Level:</strong> Shadow Route Sense, Dead Drop Specialist.</li><li><strong>3rd Level:</strong> Between-the-Moments, Courier’s Dash.</li><li><strong>5th Level:</strong> Operation Ghost Dividend, Vanish on the Wire.</li><li><strong>6th–7th Levels:</strong> Ghost-Walker’s Balance, Trace Erasure, Route Encryption.</li><li><strong>8th–10th Levels:</strong> Blinkstep Feint, Signal in the Static, Phantom Network Liaison.</li><li><strong>11th–14th Levels:</strong> Evasive Echo, Momentum Shear, Quantum Breadcrumbs, Courier’s Resilience, Horizon Thread.</li><li><strong>17th–18th Levels:</strong> Dimensional Flicker, Ghostline Anchor, Entangled Lifeline, Route Sever Paradox.</li><li><strong>20th Level:</strong> The Message Always Arrives.</li></ul><p>Phantom Couriers shine wherever routes are dangerous, information is fragile, and survival hinges on whether someone can get there <em>in time</em>—or slightly before time notices them arriving.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
